            <ArticleTitle>Reticulated phototoxic eruption in a patient on long-term diltiazem therapy.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>792-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Diltiazem hydrochloride is a commonly prescribed medication in the treatment of cardiovascular disease. A case of diltiazem-induced hyperpigmentation in a patient after significant sun exposure is reported. The morphological appearance was reticulated and slate-gray to blue in color. The pathogenesis of the hyperpigmentation is discussed and possible treatment options are reviewed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
